b6f0e9c7-3427-4fa7-9f24-435d899666ea"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"2dfd9c364972d63d66ae18ccf3e6031ae74ad3338cf27ab3587088e5d4ecf696","event_uuid":"f656d110-2565-42a9-be63-ceba5a9ed5f5","position":{"commit_sha":"768873355e5d9566147734802582c8c4f24969a6","position":"1793379828107317166-f656d110-2565-42a9-be63-ceba5a9ed5f5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"0cf68831a21ba50414ebf7b267a0f7e4afc0fe5137de055c459b3df03a763e87","event_uuid":"e4f9bb22-2003-4d70-b1cb-57d12e464c51","position":{"commit_sha":"01943bf7eb6d425c33bd10ff7b2302be7e408d58","position":"1793379904701388646-e4f9bb22-2003-4d70-b1cb-57d12e464c51"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"3b51d2df208a9f99c97a3c2afee942ef438dc8bbfe700395c78ed371c6fcca1f","event_uuid":"2ba095dd-d0fc-476b-8e37-c68d35839e2b","position":{"commit_sha":"2f5bdf85bd9018af863a4362c90c6e8bde799d01","position":"1793379941234558315-2ba095dd-d0fc-476b-8e37-c68d35839e2b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1793377691239868031,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f656d110-2565-42a9-be63-ceba5a9ed5f5","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"db2c-3a4b-1826-451f"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`src/rebar/_engine_support/resolver.py` re-exports 9 names from `rebar._ids` and adds no\nbehavior. ADR 0111 forbids internal shims: a second import path for one set of objects\nmakes every call site ambiguous about where resolution actually lives, and the shim's own\ndocstring records it as transitional.\n\nThis slice deletes it. The prerequisite story `peckish-marmatite-cuckoo` has already\nrepointed the 9 consumers that reach the shim dynamically — submodule imports used as\n`monkeypatch` targets, dotted attribute calls, and one patch-target string. Everything\nleft is a single mechanical shape.\n\n## Census\n\nMeasured on `origin/main` at `50d5a36539d` by two independent instruments that agree:\nan AST pass (`ast.ImportFrom` with relative-import resolution) and\n`git grep -lF 'from rebar._engine_support.resolver import'`. The grep matches 43 files;\none is the shim itself, whose hit is prose in its own docstring at `:8`, not an import.\n\n**42 consumer files**, every one using `from rebar._engine_support.resolver import <name>`:\n30 under `src/`, 11 under `tests/`, 1 under `scripts/`\n(`scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py`). The 30 `src/` files span `_commands/` (12),\n`_engine_support/` (6), `llm/` (8), and 4 singletons — `_lib_writes.py`, `audit/read.py`,\n`metrics/blame.py`, `signing.py`, `review_bot/artifact_emit.py`.\n\nThe counting history is worth stating, because this ticket has already been re-measured\nthree times. A line-oriented grep misses a name inside a multi-line parenthesized import.\nAn import-only AST census misses attribute access and string literals. A census keyed on\nthe full dotted module path misses `from rebar._engine_support import resolver`, where the\ntarget appears as an alias under its parent package. The 42 above survives all three\nfailure modes because it is the intersection of a shape-complete AST walk and a\nfixed-string file grep.\n\n## Change\n\n1. Rewrite the import statement in each of the 42 files from\n   `rebar._engine_support.resolver` to `rebar._ids`. The imported names and every call\n   site are unchanged — `rebar._ids` is where these objects are already defined, so this\n   removes an indirection rather than retargeting one.\n2. Delete `src/rebar/_engine_support/resolver.py`.\n3. Update `docs/bash-migration.md:168`, which names the shim as the id-resolution seam for\n   ported commands. It describes the shape current code follows, so leaving it would make\n   a live doc point at a deleted module.\n4. Add a `docs/release-notes.md` entry. The shim is private, but that file's stated scope\n   is anything \"observed by an agent or a different rebar version\", and an import of the\n   private path stops resolving here with no forwarding alias.\n\nThere is no oracle test enumerating the shim's exports and no packaged index referencing\nit; `git grep -nF '_engine_support/resolver'` finds only the archive line below.\n\n## Testing\n\nNo behavior changes, so the existing suite is the oracle: the 42 files import the same\nnames from the module that already defines them. `make verify` runs the full gating\nselection. The grep-based criteria below are what prove the deletion is complete rather\nthan partial, which is the actual failure mode for a migration of this shape.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] **AC1** `test -e src/rebar/_engine_support/resolver.py` exits 1.\n- [ ] **AC2** `git grep -F 'from rebar._engine_support.resolver import'` exits 1 with no\n      output.\n- [ ] **AC3** `git grep -nF 'rebar._engine_support.resolver'` returns exactly 2 lines,\n      both in `docs/archive/tier-e-execution-plan.md`.\n- [ ] **AC4** `git grep -nF '_engine_support/resolver'` returns exactly 1 line, in\n      `docs/archive/tier-e-execution-plan.md`.\n- [ ] **AC5** `docs/bash-migration.md` contains `rebar._ids` at the seam paragraph and no\n      longer contains `_engine_support.resolver`.\n- [ ] **AC6** `docs/release-notes.md` gains one new `##` section naming\n      `rebar._engine_support.resolver` and `rebar._ids`.\n- [ ] **AC7** `python -c 'import rebar'` exits 0.\n- [ ] **AC8** `python -c 'import rebar._engine_support.resolver'` exits non-zero with\n      `ModuleNotFoundError`.\n- [ ] **AC9** `ruff check src tests scripts` exits 0 with no output.\n- [ ] **AC10** `make typecheck` exits 0.\n- [ ] **AC11** `make verify` exits 0.\n- [ ] **AC12** `git diff --name-only origin/main...HEAD` lists exactly 45 paths: the 42\n      rewritten files, the deleted shim, `docs/bash-migration.md`, and\n      `docs/release-notes.md`.\n\n## Ordering\n\nDepends on `peckish-marmatite-cuckoo`, which must land first. That story repoints the 9\ndynamic consumers while the shim still exists; deleting the shim before it lands would\nbreak them. Independent of `censurable-exotic-snake`.\n\n## Out of scope — checked, not merely unexamined\n\n- **The 2 `docs/archive/tier-e-execution-plan.md` references (`:18`, `:77`, `:120`).**\n  Deliberately left. That file is a historical record of a completed migration tier and\n  describes the tree as it stood then; rewriting it would falsify the record. AC3 and AC4\n  pin them so a later reader sees they were considered.\n- **The 9 dynamic consumers**, all on `peckish-marmatite-cuckoo`.\n- **`rebar._ids` itself.** No signature, behavior, or export change.\n- **`rebar._engine_support`'s other modules.** `commit_impact`, `descendants`,\n  `field_reads`, `lookups`, `next_batch`, `reads`, and `reads_cli` are real\n  implementations, not shims, and stay. Only `resolver.py` is a pure re-export.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py","reason":"Rewrite import to rebar._ids"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py","reason":"Rewrite import to rebar._ids"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py","reason":"Rewrite import to rebar._ids"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/close_scope.py","reason":"Rewrite import to rebar._ids"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/compact.py","reason":"Rewrite import to rebar._ids"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/composer.py","reason":"Rewrite import to rebar._ids"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py","reason":"Rewrite import to rebar._ids"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/delete.py","reason":"Rewrite import to rebar._ids"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/link_revert.py","reason":"Rewrite import to rebar._ids"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/transition.py","reason":"Rewrite import to rebar._ids"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py","reason":"Rewrite import to rebar._ids"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/unlink.py","reason":"Rewrite import to rebar._ids"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/verify_commit.py","reason":"Rewrite import to rebar._ids"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/commit_impact.py","reason":"Rewrite import to rebar._ids"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/field_reads.py","reason":"Rewrite import to rebar._ids"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/lookups.py","reason":"Rewrite import to rebar._ids"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/next_batch.py","reason":"Rewrite import to rebar._ids"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py","reason":"Rewrite import to rebar._ids"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/reads_cli.py","reason":"Rewrite import to rebar._ids"},{"path":"src/rebar/_lib_writes.py","reason":"Rewrite import to rebar._ids"},{"path":"src/rebar/audit/read.py","reason":"Rewrite import to rebar._ids"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/code_review/assemble.py","reason":"Rewrite import to rebar._ids"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/code_review/bugfix_size_gate.py","reason":"Rewrite import to rebar._ids"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/code_review/finalize.py","reason":"Rewrite import to rebar._ids"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/code_review/sidecar.py","reason":"Rewrite import to rebar._ids"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/completion_sidecar.py","reason":"Rewrite import to rebar._ids"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/gate_runs.py","reason":"Rewrite import to rebar._ids"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py","reason":"Rewrite import to rebar._ids"},{"path":"src/rebar/metri